cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BayMorph in your research, please cite the software using this metadata."
title: "BayMorph"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cannarozzo"
    given-names: "Carlo"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-07-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/carlocannarozzophd/BayMorph"
abstract: >-
  BayMorph is a Python package for Bayesian morphological modelling of
  astronomical images, with configuration-driven image preparation, empirical
  PSF construction, Sérsic modelling, nested-sampling inference, and diagnostic
  workflows.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - galaxy morphology
  - Bayesian inference
  - nested sampling
  - Sérsic model
